📦 LINUX PACKAGE MANAGEMENT — ULTRA CHEAT SHEET (APT / dpkg / .deb)
🧠 CORE IDEA

Linux software installs come from 3 sources:

1. Official APT repositories
2. Local .deb files
3. External APT repositories (e.g. Docker)

📦 1. OFFICIAL REPOSITORY (NORMAL WAY)
apt install <package>
Example:
apt install vim curl
How it works:
Downloads from Kali/Debian repos
Fully maintained by OS
Auto-updates via apt upgrade
❌ Limitation:
Package must exist in repo
❌ Example failure:
apt install rustscan
# Unable to locate package rustscan


📄 2. LOCAL .DEB FILE INSTALL (MANUAL)
⭐ Modern recommended method:
apt install ./package.deb
⚙️ Legacy method:
dpkg -i package.deb
apt -f install
Example:
apt install ./rustscan_2.4.1-1_amd64.deb
✔ Pros:
Works without internet repo
Simple offline install
❌ Cons:
No automatic updates
Manual downloads required
⚙️ dpkg (LOW-LEVEL TOOL)
dpkg -i file.deb
What it does:
Installs .deb directly
DOES NOT resolve dependencies
Fix errors:
apt -f install


🏪 3. EXTERNAL APT REPOSITORY (DOCKER METHOD)
Step 1 — Add repo:
nano /etc/apt/sources.list.d/docker.sources
Types: deb
URIs: https://download.docker.com/linux/debian
Suites: trixie
Components: stable
Architectures: amd64
Signed-By: /etc/apt/keyrings/docker.gpg
Step 2 — Add GPG key:
curl -fsSL https://download.docker.com/linux/debian/gpg \
| gpg --dearmor -o /etc/apt/keyrings/docker.gpg
Step 3 — Install:
apt update
apt install docker-ce
✔ Pros:
Auto updates
Clean install
Fully integrated into system
⚠ Cons:
Trust external vendor

🔥 COMPARISON TABLE
Repo install     → apt install pkg        → official store → updates YES
Local .deb       → apt install ./file     → manual file    → updates NO
dpkg             → dpkg -i file           → low-level      → risky
External repo    → apt install pkg        → added store    → updates YES
🧩 REAL EXAMPLE (RUSTSCAN)
❌ Failed:
apt install rustscan

Reason: not in Kali repos

❌ Wrong attempts:
9-byte download (HTML error)
ZIP renamed as .deb
✅ Correct:
apt install ./rustscan_2.4.1-1_amd64.deb


🧠 FINAL MENTAL MODEL
APT sources:
1. Official repos
2. Local .deb files
3. External vendor repos
🚀 KEY TAKEAWAYS
.deb = installer file (like .exe)
dpkg = low-level installer (no dependency handling)
apt install ./file.deb = modern safe install
apt install pkg = repo-based install
Docker method = adding new software store to APT
